From 9d3cf0e8be245fabe475002184e4dcb81b026379 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vita-build <vita@build>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:52:04 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Vita: decals again (depth pass then colour, no-discard
 program in both, PS1 order kept), texture decoding on 3 more cores

- t24 drew batched opaque faces in one pass and decals flickered (skatepark graffiti, lighting):
  without the depth pass a decal and the surface under it tie. The depth pass is back (t20-t23's
  depth then colour within 1/256), with t24's no-discard program in both passes for the faces
  that can take it. The colour pass draws the opaque faces in the PS1's order across the two
  programs (runs of one program, up to 48; [gl] line: colour runs), so the later of a decal and
  its floor is still the one left. THPS_R3D_PREPASS=0: t24's one pass. THPS_R3D_ZNUDGE=1 (a
  trial): one pass with each opaque view-space face of a layer scaled nearer by up to 1/256 of
  its depth in the PS1's order (same pixels, nearer depth). Boot line: "[r3d] opaque batches".
- Texture cache pages are decoded by the game thread and up to 3 threads on cores 1-3 (bands of
  rows; core 3 needs CapUnlocker, else cores 1-2), waited for before the page is drawn. t24's
  level start decoded 117 pages in 921 ms on the game thread. THPS_GL_DECODE_THREADS=n (0: the
  game thread alone); boot line "[gl] texture decode threads".
---
 platform/pc/README.md           |   4 +-
 platform/pc/include/pc/gl_gpu.h |  17 ++-
 platform/pc/src/pc_gpu_gl.cpp   | 253 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 3 files changed, 225 insertions(+), 49 deletions(-)

